dict(slug='about', title='An independent proposal, open to useful participation', nav='About the project',
     eyebrow='Luke Nathan Hayes · Minjerribah · Australia',
     lead='Personal agency and shared capability give the work its purpose. Evidence and actual relationships give it a path forward.',
     description='Author, purpose, development stage, accessibility and privacy of the Aura disaster resilience companion website.',
     chapters=[], body='''
<section><h2>About Aura of Intelligence</h2>
<p><a href="https://github.com/auraofintelligence/open-record-luke-nathan-hayes/tree/main">Luke Nathan Hayes</a> is developing Aura of Intelligence as a personal AI operating system and adaptive whole-of-life support direction. The disaster proposal brings qualified self development, self-sovereign records and practical learning into a dependable community-service ambition.</p>
<p>GAJRA Earth, the <strong>Global Association for Joyful Responsible Abundance on Earth</strong>, supplies a values starting point. The work is open to local interpretation, disagreement and improvement. Public information and essential assistance remain independent of pledges or association enrolment. [P1]</p>
<p>This is Luke’s independent proposal. Organisations named as sources retain their own responsibilities. References to Council, QIT Plus, public agencies, hospitals, the Olympics or other projects establish no partnership, appointment, funding or endorsement.</p></section>
<section><h2>What is available, and what comes next.</h2>
<p>The public document, research repository, wiki, associated source publications and this companion website are available to examine. Aura Matrix Studio supplies current browser-tool foundations. An integrated, protected and dependable disaster service still needs demonstrations, technical work, actual hosts, resources, qualified input and service relationships.</p>
<p>The new <a href="connected-capability.html">Missing Middle</a> and <a href="practice.html#escape-rooms">escape-room</a> connections broaden practical opportunities to investigate. They do not turn proposals into operating installations or programmes.</p></section>
<section id="site-privacy"><h2>Using this website</h2>
<p>These are static reading pages. They contain no account registration, advertising, analytics scripts, personal onboarding form or live assistance inbox. Page search runs in the browser against the site’s reading index. The interest-note builder, where used, keeps text in the current page until you copy or download it; it sends nothing.</p>
<p>GitHub Pages serves the site and has its own platform practices. Following an outside link takes you to that provider. For the proposed system’s personal-data model, read <a href="personal-aura.html#ownership">self-sovereign data</a>; those design commitments are separate from a claim that this publication hosts a protected personal Aura.</p></section>
<section><h2>Reading and imagery</h2>
<p>Pages use responsive text, keyboard navigation, a skip link, semantic headings, image descriptions and reduced-motion support. The full document is also available as PDF, Word and HTML text. Feedback on an access barrier is welcome through the project repository.</p>
<p>Illustrations are AI-generated concepts commissioned for this website. They depict imagined scenes and equipment, with captions identifying that status. They are neither photographs of deployed Aura services nor evidence of test results. The <a href="assets/image-provenance.json">image provenance record</a> preserves prompts and asset details.</p>
<p>Website edition: 30 October 2026. Foundational document: 27 October 2026. <a href="licence.html">Licence and crawler information</a> explain reuse and discovery.</p></section>
'''),
